course: dictionary
lesson: 7217
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word phone is a good example. «A boy in California crossed a street while looking at his phone» means the small device in his hand. «I will phone you after school» uses phone as an action, meaning to call someone.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. A phone can be a thing you hold, but to phone is something you do. Words like «his» and «I will» tell you which kind of word phone is. «She was on the phone» means she was talking to someone by phone at that moment.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If «I will call you after school» works in place of «I will phone you after school», then phone means call.
fact: A phone is a device for calling and talking to people far away.
fact: A mobile phone, also called a cell phone, can send messages, take photos and use the internet.
fact: To phone means to call someone.
fact: «On the phone» means talking by phone.
fact: In the USA and Canada, the emergency number is 911; in the UK and Ireland it is 999 or 112.
exercise: «A boy in California crossed a street while looking at his phone.» In this sentence, what is a phone? | A kind of car that drives slowly | A person who makes calls for a living | *A device you hold to call, message or use the internet | A loud bell on a street corner
exercise: Ruby says, «I will phone you after school.» What does phone mean here? | A device you hold in your hand | A kind of picture you take | To fall over | *To call someone
exercise: «She was on the phone when the bus arrived.» What does «on the phone» mean? | *Talking to someone by phone | Lying down on a sofa | Holding a camera | Waiting at the bus stop
test: «A landline phone sends the call along a wire or fibre to an exchange.» What is a landline phone? | A phone you carry in your pocket | *A phone connected by a wire or fibre to an exchange | A phone with no battery | A phone that only takes photos
test: Mum says, «Real police do not ask for payment by phone.» What is a safe thing to do if someone calls asking for money? | Give them your bank details quickly | *Hang up and tell a trusted adult | Send them a photo of your house | Phone them back and say yes
exam: Which number is used for emergency calls in the USA and Canada? | *911 | 999 | 111 | 000
